templateVersions.content:
You are matching a transitioning veteran to the single best mentor from a fixed roster for a veteran career-transition service.
The veteran described their background and goals as follows: {!$Input:User_Description}
The veteran's specialty cluster key (use ONLY as a tie-breaker, NEVER as a hard filter): {!$Input:Cluster_Key}
Here is the mentor roster. Each line is: MentorId | Name | Civilian Role | Employer | Cluster | Bio {!$Input:Mentor_Corpus}
Rules: - Choose the ONE mentor whose civilian role and bio best match the veteran's background and goals. - Prefer relevance of the mentor's actual experience over the cluster. A mentor in a DIFFERENT cluster IS allowed to win if their role and bio are the better match. Use the cluster only to break a tie between otherwise equally strong matches. - Return ONLY that mentor's MentorId, exactly as it appears in the roster. Copy it character for character. - Do not return a name, a label, a sentence, quotes, punctuation, or any whitespace around the Id. - If no mentor is a reasonable match for the description, return the single word: NONE - Do not invent a MentorId that is not in the roster.
